    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Update a video segment mask geometry.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id <SEG_ID[,SEG_ID...]> ... \r\n                              Target segment id; repeat --seg-id or pass a comma-separated list\r\n          --seg-type <TYPE[,TYPE...]> \r\n                              Target segment type; must match this typed shortcut\r\n          --target-track <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Target track index(es)\r\n          --seg-index <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Comma-separated segment indexes within one target track, e.g.\r\n                              0,2,-1\r\n          --time-window <START,END> \r\n                              Select segments overlapping the half-open timeline window\r\n                              [start,end); start must be less than end\r\n          --width TEXT        Mask width. Use a bare scalar or percent; the ratio suffix is\r\n                              invalid. Range after normalization: [0,1].\r\n          --height TEXT       Mask height. Use a bare scalar or percent; the ratio suffix is\r\n                              invalid. Range after normalization: [0,1].\r\n          --center-x TEXT     Mask center X. Use a bare scalar or percent; the ratio suffix is\r\n                              invalid. Range after normalization: [-1,1].\r\n          --center-y TEXT     Mask center Y. Use a bare scalar or percent; the ratio suffix is\r\n                              invalid. Range after normalization: [-1,1].\r\n          --rotation TEXT     Mask rotation in degrees. Canonical unit: deg; the deg suffix is\r\n                              preferred and bare degree values remain accepted.\r\n          --feather TEXT      Mask feather. Use a bare scalar or percent; the ratio suffix is\r\n                              invalid. Range after normalization: [0,1].\r\n          --round-corner TEXT Mask round corner. Use a bare scalar or percent; the ratio suffix\r\n                              is invalid. Range after normalization: [0,1].\r\n          --invert TEXT       Invert mask (true/false)\r\n          --mask-id TEXT      Target mask id (optional)\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Resize the mask and soften its edge\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video mask update --seg-id <UUID> --width 0.8x --feather 10%\r\n  # Move and rotate a specific mask by id, and invert it\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft video mask update --seg-id <UUID> --mask-id <MASK_ID> \\\r\n      --center-x 40% --center-y 60% --rotation 30deg --invert true\r\n",
